<h1>Linux User Net</h1>

<p class="lun-intro">Links read on the Monday Night Linux User Net —
Mondays, 8:10–9:00 PM Pacific, on the
<a href="https://arrg.org">ARRG</a> K7RPT repeater system.
<a href="/lun/info/">About the net</a>
· <a href="/lun/archive/">Archive</a>
· <a href="/lun/feed.xml">Feed</a>
· <a href="https://groups.io/g/the-linux-user-net/topics">Discuss on groups.io</a></p>

<p>Each week below collects the news items discussed during that
Monday's session. The net has been on the air for about ten years, and
this list exists because people kept it week after week: stewards of
the earliest years whose records I haven't found, then
<strong>Mark, KC7NYR</strong> —
<a href="https://www.kc7nyr.com/">kc7nyr.com</a> carries the list back
to early 2022 — and <strong>Russ, KC7MM</strong>, at
<a href="https://kc7mm.com/wiki/doku.php?id=linuxusernet:linuxnews">kc7mm.com</a>.
Thanks to all of them, equally. If you hold pieces of the early
history, <a href="https://groups.io/g/the-linux-user-net/topics">the
groups.io forum</a> would welcome them.</p>

